{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542560-101-dead-families","id":1542560,"title":"101 Dead Families","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-24T10:55:23-07:00","id":1542560,"title":"101 Dead Families","content":"After reading about the Dead more with the previews I thought I'd try my hand at making a few more Dead Families.<br /> <br /> Name of the game is to post a Family idea and continue the numbering on from the previous post/reply. Like so:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Amalgams</b> - This family tries to reframe from getting new bodies and instead do physical repairs on their corpses until they are completely worn out. Sometimes known as the Scarred due to the stitches that are often shown where they've tried to repair cuts. Emotional association is Nostalgia.</li> <li><b>Theseus/Frankensteins</b>- This family are dead that will repair their bodies with parts from other corpses. They try to hold on to their original form as much as possible, but replace parts as they wear out. They are less likely to patch themselves up than to replace their own body parts. Emotional association is with Envy.</li> <li><b>Galatean/Collodi </b>- This family of dead only inhabit inanimate objects such as mannequins and statues. Some of the newer ones will keep their old bodies, but when the bodies give way they try to reframe from using human corpses without consent. Emotional association is with Joy.</li> <li><b>Gremlins </b>- This faimly of dead has an affinity for possessing objects of any type. Typically they don't anchor themselves to objects for long periods of time, but some have. They tend to use their possession of inanimate objects to haunt people and cause technology to fail around their targets. Emotional association is with Stress.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T11:15:06-07:00","id":1542562,"title":"","content":"Reading your Galatean/Collodi, I can't help but think of a faction from Planescape, I don't remember their name but they would pay people in order to acquire legal rights to their corpse once they were dead. <br /> <br /> 5. Bestia - This family specialized in possessing animals. Some do so because they view dead human remains as unclean, others do so simply because they were furries in life. Their emotional association is disgust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T11:37:36-07:00","id":1542563,"title":"","content":"6. The Exalted Dead. This dead family has its origins in a mortal cult of ancient Egypt. They preserved the bodies of the dead to give those important deceased people power in the afterlife. This process, of course, is mummification. When the proper rituals have been performed, the dead has special powers, including the ability to animate the preserved corpse. They draw power from veneration, worship, great respect or adoration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}